# This repo has no root-level app of its own — real env files live in
# apps/web/.env, apps/cms/.env, and apps/api/.env (copy the matching
# *.env.example* in each). This file only documents .env.local.
#
# Once the repo is linked to the Neon project (see README.md "Neon setup"),
# `neon link` and `neon deploy` write a repo-root `.env.local` containing the
# linked branch's live DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED, NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL,
# NEON_AUTH_JWKS_URL, and AWS_* (object storage) values. `apps/api`'s dev
# server and its db:migrate / db:seed / auth:create-editor scripts load that
# file automatically.
#
# .env.local is gitignored (see .gitignore's `*.local` rule) and regenerated
# by the Neon CLI — never create or commit it by hand.
